@startuml mf-02a-reserve-aim
' SRS Section II.1.2.2 — Main Workflow: Delivery, part A (Reserve & Aim)
' Continues in mf-02b-commit-dropoff-retreat.puml
' Supersedes mf-02a-approach.puml: the approach leg (TO2) was retired when the
' drop-off slot became dynamic — the vehicle is aimed at its own slot instead.
' Business-level vocabulary only; implementation detail belongs in the SDS.
' Render: java -jar plantuml.jar -charset UTF-8 -tpng mf-02a-reserve-aim.puml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam swimlaneWidth 260
skinparam ArrowColor #000000
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #000000
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #7ACFF4
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #000000
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #7ACFF4
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #7ACFF4
skinparam NoteBorderColor #000000

|FMS (openTCS)|
|WES|
|AGV|

|FMS (openTCS)|
start
:The pick-up transport order\nreaches FINISHED;
:Notify WES;
note left: WES re-checks order state on a heartbeat,\nso a lost notification does not stall the task

|WES|
:Receive the pick-up completion;
if (Drop-off order already issued?) then (Yes)
  :Ignore the duplicate notification;
  stop
else (No)
endif
if (Assigned vehicle and\ndestination zone both present?) then (No)
  :Task -> FAILED;
  stop
else (Yes)
endif
:Take exclusive access\nto the zone's slot map;
:Reserve one concrete drop-off slot\nby the cascading depth-first fill rule (BR-11),\ncounting the slots already committed\nand the slots already reserved;
if (Any slot free to reserve?) then (No)
  :Release the zone;
  :Stay in PICKING_UP;\nthe periodic re-check retries;
  stop
else (Yes)
endif
:Record the reserved slot on the cargo;
:Release the zone;
note right: A reservation is provisional -\nanother vehicle may still take the slot
:Resolve the 2-cell retreat path\nbehind the reserved slot;
if (Retreat path found?) then (No)
  :Log a warning - the drop-off order\ngoes out without the retreat steps;
else (Yes)
endif
:Issue the drop-off transport order\naimed at the reserved slot:\nunload at the slot, then one move step\nper retreat cell;
:Task -> DELIVERING;
note right: Each vehicle drives straight to a slot of its own -\nthere is no shared approach point, so two vehicles\nare never routed to the same destination

|FMS (openTCS)|
:Route the vehicle\ntowards the reserved slot;

|AGV|
:Drive towards the destination zone;
stop
note right: Continues in part B\n(Commit, Drop-off & Retreat)

@enduml
